Set-Location -LiteralPath $PSScriptRoot
$msg = 'security: a super_admin on one brand could read and overwrite another brand customer Twilio credentials. Three routers resolved an organization from a QUERY parameter for anyone holding super_admin, loading it by id alone with no platform comparison - org_settings_router._resolve_org feeding 13 endpoints including PUT /org-settings/twilio which writes org_twilio_account_sid and the encrypted auth token, settings_router._resolve_appt_org feeding 3 read and write endpoints, and an inline copy in crm_native_router. require_super_admin proves the caller is A platform operator; it says nothing about WHICH platform. load_org_in_scope already existed for exactly this and its own comment says every route accepting an org_id must go through it - these three took the id as a query parameter rather than a path parameter, which is how they were missed. All three now route through that existing guard rather than a second authorization system: god_admin still reaches every org on every platform, a super_admin is confined to their own platform, a customer org_admin never enters the branch, and refusal is 404 not 403 so another brand customer list cannot be enumerated one id at a time. Adds scripts/probe_org_settings_scoping.py as its own deploy gate: two platforms, a super_admin each, a god above both and a customer org_admin, with every REFUSED check paired with an ALLOWED check so a guard that refuses everything cannot pass. Verified by reverting the fix and re-running - the gate reports 6 leaks including Brand B stored Account SID being overwritten, which confirms the write was live rather than theoretical - then restoring. Payloads are schema-valid on purpose, because an invalid one 422s during validation before the org is resolved and would let the gate pass while the boundary was open. Sweep section 32 adds the static half so the shape cannot reappear in a fourth router, and asserts the new gate does not swallow the platform-boundary gate beside it. No change to Restland, EvoSys, branding or the BookaBoost migration.'
& "$PSScriptRoot\deploy.ps1" -Message $msg
Write-Output ("DEPLOY_EXIT=" + $LASTEXITCODE)
